{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "11", "m": "09", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "23", "M": "38", "S": "40"}}, "news": [{"title": "Construction of houses for Wayanad rehabilitation to be completed by Oct-end: Minister", "para": "The construction of homes in the Wayanad rehabilitation township is on track, with a completion date set for the end of October. The contractor is focused on delivering all 110 houses as planned. Additionally, a review will allow for the inclusion of disaster victims initially overlooked. By December, basic infrastructure work will be completed, followed by a beneficiary selection process via a draw.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/construction-of-houses-for-wayanad-rehabilitation-to-be-completed-by-oct-end-minister/134050698?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-311712/134050698.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Patna civic body launches 15-day drive to recover \u20b980 crore property tax due", "para": "The Patna Municipal Corporation has launched a dedicated fifteen-day campaign to assess property taxes. This initiative focuses on incorporating unassessed properties while also re-evaluating existing ones. The goal is to recover around eighty crore rupees in outstanding tax payments. Special teams will prioritize new assessments and target major defaulters, utilizing electricity consumer data to discover properties that have evaded taxation.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/patna-civic-body-launches-15-day-drive-to-recover-80-crore-property-tax-due/134050632?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-142866/134050632.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Delhi: Only three PG buildings out of 1,355 found 'visibly dangerous' in MCD survey, nine found repairable", "para": "The Municipal Corporation of Delhi has conducted a survey revealing three hazardous paying-guest buildings, housing a total of sixty-nine residents who urgently need relocation. Additionally, nine more structures were marked for substantial repairs. Reflecting heightened vigilance post the recent collapse in Satya Niketan, authorities have demolished 111 properties and sealed off 88 within just four days.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/delhi-only-three-pg-buildings-out-of-1355-found-visibly-dangerous-in-mcd-survey-nine-found-repairable/134050497?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-45884/134050497.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}]}